       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and a 1,700 mg single dose is also above the usual maximum single dose. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is significant, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- Another dose. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, please confirm it. I can enter it with a note saying you've confirmed the dose.\n\nTell me which one and I'll enter it right away."
